                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[b]I hate this game, but I love it.[/b]\nThis is one of those games that can be frustrating and enjoyable at the same time.\n\nThe random questions and events are probably what annoy me the most. Half the time I pick the right answer, and the other half I get it wrong. It often feels more like luck than anything else (really there is no logic).\n\nThat said, the game itself isn't particularly difficult once you figure out how to manage your money.\n\nMy advice is to stay in the first world you unlock and keep crafting weapons for its heroes until you've saved a few million. It might feel repetitive, but it makes the rest of the game much more comfortable. Once money stops being a concern, you can take your time exploring, experimenting with weapons, upgrading your shop, and adjusting your strategy without constantly worrying about expenses.\n\n[b]The game rewards patience more than skill.[/b] You don't need a complicated strategy to succeed, just a good financial foundation early on.\n\nThere are some annoying mechanics, and the repetition can get tiring, but there's also something oddly satisfying about running your little weapon shop and watching it grow.\n\n[i]It's not a difficult game, and it's certainly not perfect, but despite all the things that irritate me, I still had (and will still have) a good time with it.[/i] I'm going for the missing achievements of the expansion so.... yeap.\n\n[b]Recommended, especially if you enjoy casual management games and don't mind a bit of grinding.[/b]",
